   "relative_headroom_reasoning": "AK(2) ran at 15 = 11 + 4; AK(3) runs at 17 = 13 + 4.  Both runs give the operator the same additive slack above their root's scale (any relator may grow to root-total + 4 letters), keeping the per-pop expansion geometry comparable; the matched quantities are the operator and the 1,000-pop budget.",
   "absolute_cap_argument": "An ABSOLUTE match (cap 15 for both) would leave AK(3) only 2 letters of headroom above its 13-letter root versus AK(2)'s 4, mechanically suppressing child generation and biasing the control toward zero hits.  Cap 17 makes the AK(3) box strictly LARGER (per-relator <= 17 vs <= 15) -- the conservative direction: a zero-hit outcome cannot be attributed to a smaller search space."
